& [Threats]
  + [RIS-T01] either seed root is missing duplicated mis-kinded or identity-colliding
  + [RIS-T02] a nonroot has no producer multiple producers or a producer whose expected output differs
  + [RIS-T03] a root is produced, a graph cycle exists, or a node is unreachable from both roots
  + [RIS-T04] request order affects compiled bytes or a supplied order launders a different graph
  + [RIS-T05] duplicate or case-colliding targets overwrite one another
  + [RIS-T06] traversal drive UNC device alternate-stream backslash empty dot dot-dot link or overbound path escapes the logical layout
  + [RIS-T07] mutable locator ambient PATH environment current directory cache network or undeclared tool becomes a hidden input
  + [RIS-T08] supplied digest is interpreted as provenance license trust compatibility safety suitability availability or successful acquisition
  + [RIS-T09] secret bytes enter prerequisite references machine forms evidence logs or fixtures
  + [RIS-T10] source build transform generated configuration and acquired artifact roles collapse and obscure provenance
  + [RIS-T11] overflow count depth bytes text node edge input prerequisite evidence or material-byte totals evade bounds
  + [RIS-T12] request plan or receipt self-digest includes itself or uses a nondomain-separated digest
  + [RIS-T13] an expected receipt is reported as an observed installation or activation receipt
  + [RIS-T14] fully redigested semantic tampering passes a manifest-only verifier
  + [RIS-T15] compiler or verifier touches filesystem environment clock process network provider model MCP Git workspace remote or hardware state
  + [RIS-T16] existing seeded-compiler candidate PreparedRuntime or boot-session forms are relabeled as completed runtime inflation
  + [RIS-T17] foreign dirty files enter attribution or publication

& [Controls]
  + strict canonical parser exact two-root cardinality distinct SemanticIds closed enums finite checked arithmetic producer and reachability proofs deterministic normalization conservative paths exact authority denials typed faults all-zero effect counters independent recompilation semantic tamper tests and exact staged inventory

& [TypedFaultVocabulary]
  + malformed_json unknown_field duplicate_field trailing_data overbound depth_overflow text_invalid identifier_invalid digest_invalid count_invalid bytes_overflow root_cardinality root_kind_mismatch identity_collision node_missing producer_missing producer_duplicate root_has_producer input_missing input_duplicate output_mismatch graph_cycle unreachable_node target_invalid target_collision source_invalid mutable_locator ambient_input secret_material prerequisite_invalid authority_mismatch request_digest_mismatch plan_digest_mismatch receipt_template_mismatch verification_mismatch effect_nonzero
